course: dictionary
lesson: 284
title: Two meanings in one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ammonite is an extinct sea animal with a coiled shell. Extinct means it died out long ago and no longer lives anywhere. Context helps you here: «Ammonites were sea creatures with coiled shells, related to squid, and are very common fossils.» Sea creatures, coiled shells and fossils are all clues that the word names an animal.
explain: The same word can also mean the fossil of that animal, the stone spiral left in rock. Read the sentence to find out which meaning fits: «Fossil hunters look for ammonites on the beach» means the stones, because you cannot go looking for a living animal in the rocks. Ask yourself what the word is doing in the sentence.
explain: Words can also tell you about time. «They died out at the same time as the big dinosaurs» tells you ammonites lived long before us. Died out means stopped existing, with none left alive. Put your meaning into the sentence to check: if it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: An ammonite is an extinct sea animal with a coiled shell.
fact: «Ammonite» can also mean the fossil of that animal, a stone spiral found in rocks.
fact: Ammonites are related to today's octopus, squid and nautilus.
fact: «Died out» means stopped existing, with none left alive.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and it can show you which meaning of a word is correct.
exercise: «Ammonites were sea creatures with coiled shells, related to squid.» What is an ammonite? | *A sea animal with a coiled shell | A kind of tree | A large bird that lives on cliffs | A type of sand
exercise: «They died out at the same time as the big dinosaurs.» What does died out mean? | *Stopped existing, with none left alive | Went for a long walk | Got very dirty | Moved to the sea
exercise: Ella finds a spiral stone on the beach and says, «It's an ammonite!» What has she found? | A piece of broken plastic | A pebble smoothed by the waves | *The fossil of an ancient sea animal | A live octopus
test: Which animals are ammonites related to, according to «related to octopuses and squid»? | Dinosaurs and dogs | Snails and worms | *Octopuses and squid | Whales and seals
test: «Fossil hunters keep away from cliff bottoms, where rocks fall.» Why do they keep away? | *Because rocks may fall on them | To find more shells in the sand | Because cliffs are made of sugar | To watch the waves
exam: Ammonites died out about 66 million years ago, at the same time as which animals? | Sabre-toothed cats | *The big dinosaurs | Early birds | Woolly mammoths
